{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TL;DR:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" This is a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"breaking change"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The root-level convenience sampling props on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ai()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" — have been "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"removed"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and now live inside provider-native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. Passing them at the root no longer type-checks and has no effect at runtime. Move each one into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" under its provider's canonical name (e.g. OpenAI's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":", Anthropic's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":", Gemini's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxOutputTokens"},{"type":"text","value":", Ollama's nested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.num_predict"},{"type":"text","value":"). A provider-aware codemod does the rewrite for you. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" is unaffected and stays at the root."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-changed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What changed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Previously, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" accepted three generic sampling props directly at the root of its options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 100,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These were a convenience layer that the runtime mapped onto whatever the underlying provider expected. That generic mapping is now gone. Sampling parameters live where every other model-specific knob already lives — inside the provider-native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" object — under each provider's own canonical key name."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-it-changed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why it changed"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-native, single source of truth."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Every provider names these parameters differently — OpenAI's Responses API wants "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":", Anthropic wants "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":", Gemini wants "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxOutputTokens"},{"type":"text","value":", Ollama nests them under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":". A single generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" prop had to guess the target per provider. Putting them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" means there is exactly one place sampling lives, and it matches the provider's own API surface."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" is already typed per adapter+model, so moving sampling there gives you autocomplete and compile-time checking for the exact keys a given model accepts — instead of three loosely-typed root props."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No generic mapping."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Reasoning models in particular do not treat these parameters uniformly (some ignore "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", some reject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" below the thinking budget, etc.). A generic root-level mapping papered over those differences; provider-native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" lets each adapter handle them honestly."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"before-after-by-provider","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before / after by provider"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The root prop names are the same everywhere ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":"). The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" target key differs per provider — use the exact key your provider expects."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 100,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"anthropic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 1024,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_tokens: 1024,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gemini","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: geminiText('gemini-3.1-pro-preview'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 2048,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { geminiText } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: geminiText('gemini-3.1-pro-preview'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    topP: 0.9,\n    maxOutputTokens: 2048,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ollama-nested-under-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollama (nested under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollama is the one provider where sampling parameters are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nested"}]},{"type":"text","value":" inside an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and the token limit is named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"num_predict"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: ollamaText('llama3'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 1000,\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { ollamaText } from '@tanstack/ai-ollama'\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: ollamaText('llama3'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.3,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      num_predict: 1000,\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-key-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider key reference"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Root prop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Groq"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollama (nested under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.temperature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.top_p"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxOutputTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_completion_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxCompletionTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.num_predict"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"automated-codemod","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automated codemod"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A jscodeshift codemod moves the root sampling props into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for you, renaming each one to the correct provider-native key. It resolves the provider from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter:"},{"type":"text","value":" factory call (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText('gpt-4o')"},{"type":"text","value":" → OpenAI), so the rewrite is provider-aware. Run it from the repo:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm codemod:move-sampling-to-model-options \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Or run the published transform directly — no clone needed:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npx jscodeshift \\\n  --parser=tsx \\\n  -t https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/ai/main/codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/transform.ts \\\n  \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--dry --print"},{"type":"text","value":" to preview the rewrite without modifying files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Targets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ai()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls imported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolves the provider from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter:"},{"type":"text","value":" factory call and renames each present root prop to that provider's canonical key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Ollama, nests the renamed keys inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merges into an existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" object literal when present; preserves the original value expressions and expands shorthand props ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ temperature }"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature: temperature"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Report + skip (never partial):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the codemod never partially transforms a call. It leaves the call untouched and emits an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"api.report(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" message when it can't safely proceed:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unresolvable adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"},{"type":"text","value":" prop, the adapter isn't a recognized provider-factory call (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"makeAdapter()"},{"type":"text","value":"), or it's dynamic/spread."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" is not a plain object literal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — e.g. a spread or an identifier reference."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key conflict"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — a target renamed key already exists in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" (or in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.options"},{"type":"text","value":" for Ollama). Resolve these by hand."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/README.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/README.md"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full transform details and limitations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-stays-at-the-root","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What stays at the root"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a sampling parameter and is unaffected — it stays at the root of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  metadata: { requestId: 'abc-123' }, // ← still at the root\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"need-help","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Need Help?"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/per-model-type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-Model Type Safety"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — how the adapter+model pair drives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" inference."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — complete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" signature."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See your provider's adapter page ("},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/anthropic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/gemini","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/ollama","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollama"}]},{"type":"text","value":") for the full list of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" it accepts."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-changed","text":"What changed","level":2},{"id":"why-it-changed","text":"Why it changed","level":2},{"id":"before-after-by-provider","text":"Before / after by provider","level":2},{"id":"openai","text":"OpenAI","level":3},{"id":"anthropic","text":"Anthropic","level":3},{"id":"gemini","text":"Gemini","level":3},{"id":"ollama-nested-under-options","text":"Ollama (nested under options)","level":3},{"id":"provider-key-reference","text":"Provider key reference","level":2},{"id":"automated-codemod","text":"Automated codemod","level":2},{"id":"what-stays-at-the-root","text":"What stays at the root","level":2},{"id":"need-help","text":"Need Help?","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> **TL;DR:** This is a **breaking change**. The root-level convenience sampling props on `chat()` / `ai()` / `generate()` — `temperature`, `topP`, and `maxTokens` — have been **removed** and now live inside provider-native `modelOptions` instead. Passing them at the root no longer type-checks and has no effect at runtime. Move each one into `modelOptions` under its provider's canonical name (e.g. OpenAI's `max_output_tokens`, Anthropic's `max_tokens`, Gemini's `maxOutputTokens`, Ollama's nested `options.num_predict`). A provider-aware codemod does the rewrite for you. `metadata` is unaffected and stays at the root.\n\n## What changed\n\nPreviously, `chat()` accepted three generic sampling props directly at the root of its options:\n\n```typescript ignore\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 100,\n})\n```\n\nThese were a convenience layer that the runtime mapped onto whatever the underlying provider expected. That generic mapping is now gone. Sampling parameters live where every other model-specific knob already lives — inside the provider-native `modelOptions` object — under each provider's own canonical key name.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Why it changed\n\n- **Provider-native, single source of truth.** Every provider names these parameters differently — OpenAI's Responses API wants `max_output_tokens`, Anthropic wants `max_tokens`, Gemini wants `maxOutputTokens`, Ollama nests them under `options`. A single generic `maxTokens` prop had to guess the target per provider. Putting them in `modelOptions` means there is exactly one place sampling lives, and it matches the provider's own API surface.\n- **Typed.** `modelOptions` is already typed per adapter+model, so moving sampling there gives you autocomplete and compile-time checking for the exact keys a given model accepts — instead of three loosely-typed root props.\n- **No generic mapping.** Reasoning models in particular do not treat these parameters uniformly (some ignore `temperature`, some reject `max_tokens` below the thinking budget, etc.). A generic root-level mapping papered over those differences; provider-native `modelOptions` lets each adapter handle them honestly.\n\n## Before / after by provider\n\nThe root prop names are the same everywhere (`temperature`, `topP`, `maxTokens`). The `modelOptions` target key differs per provider — use the exact key your provider expects.\n\n### OpenAI\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 100,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Anthropic\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 1024,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_tokens: 1024,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Gemini\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: geminiText('gemini-3.1-pro-preview'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 2048,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { geminiText } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: geminiText('gemini-3.1-pro-preview'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    topP: 0.9,\n    maxOutputTokens: 2048,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Ollama (nested under `options`)\n\nOllama is the one provider where sampling parameters are **nested** inside an `options` object within `modelOptions`, and the token limit is named `num_predict`:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: ollamaText('llama3'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 1000,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { ollamaText } from '@tanstack/ai-ollama'\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: ollamaText('llama3'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.3,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      num_predict: 1000,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Provider key reference\n\n| Root prop     | OpenAI              | Anthropic    | Gemini            | Grok         | Groq                    | OpenRouter            | Ollama (nested under `options`) |\n| ------------- | ------------------- | ------------ | ----------------- | ------------ | ----------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `temperature` | `temperature`       | `temperature`| `temperature`     | `temperature`| `temperature`           | `temperature`         | `options.temperature`           |\n| `topP`        | `top_p`             | `top_p`      | `topP`            | `top_p`      | `top_p`                 | `topP`                | `options.top_p`                 |\n| `maxTokens`   | `max_output_tokens` | `max_tokens` | `maxOutputTokens` | `max_tokens` | `max_completion_tokens` | `maxCompletionTokens` | `options.num_predict`           |\n\n## Automated codemod\n\nA jscodeshift codemod moves the root sampling props into `modelOptions` for you, renaming each one to the correct provider-native key. It resolves the provider from the `adapter:` factory call (e.g. `openaiText('gpt-4o')` → OpenAI), so the rewrite is provider-aware. Run it from the repo:\n\n```bash\npnpm codemod:move-sampling-to-model-options \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"\n```\n\nOr run the published transform directly — no clone needed:\n\n```bash\nnpx jscodeshift \\\n  --parser=tsx \\\n  -t https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/ai/main/codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/transform.ts \\\n  \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"\n```\n\nAdd `--dry --print` to preview the rewrite without modifying files.\n\n**What it does:**\n\n- Targets `chat()`, `ai()`, `generate()`, and `createChatOptions()` calls imported from `@tanstack/ai`.\n- Resolves the provider from the `adapter:` factory call and renames each present root prop to that provider's canonical key.\n- For Ollama, nests the renamed keys inside `modelOptions.options`.\n- Merges into an existing `modelOptions` object literal when present; preserves the original value expressions and expands shorthand props (`{ temperature }` → `temperature: temperature`).\n\n**Report + skip (never partial):** the codemod never partially transforms a call. It leaves the call untouched and emits an `api.report(...)` message when it can't safely proceed:\n\n- **Unresolvable adapter** — no `adapter` prop, the adapter isn't a recognized provider-factory call (e.g. `makeAdapter()`), or it's dynamic/spread.\n- **`modelOptions` is not a plain object literal** — e.g. a spread or an identifier reference.\n- **Key conflict** — a target renamed key already exists in `modelOptions` (or in `modelOptions.options` for Ollama). Resolve these by hand.\n\nSee [`codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/README.md`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/README.md) for the full transform details and limitations.\n\n## What stays at the root\n\n`metadata` is **not** a sampling parameter and is unaffected — it stays at the root of `chat()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  metadata: { requestId: 'abc-123' }, // ← still at the root\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Need Help?\n\n- [Per-Model Type Safety](../advanced/per-model-type-safety) — how the adapter+model pair drives `modelOptions` inference.\n- [API Reference](../api/ai) — complete `chat()` signature.\n- See your provider's adapter page ([OpenAI](../adapters/openai), [Anthropic](../adapters/anthropic), [Gemini](../adapters/gemini), [Ollama](../adapters/ollama)) for the full list of `modelOptions` it accepts.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions\n---\n\n> **TL;DR:** This is a **breaking change**. The root-level convenience sampling props on `chat()` / `ai()` / `generate()` — `temperature`, `topP`, and `maxTokens` — have been **removed** and now live inside provider-native `modelOptions` instead. Passing them at the root no longer type-checks and has no effect at runtime. Move each one into `modelOptions` under its provider's canonical name (e.g. OpenAI's `max_output_tokens`, Anthropic's `max_tokens`, Gemini's `maxOutputTokens`, Ollama's nested `options.num_predict`). A provider-aware codemod does the rewrite for you. `metadata` is unaffected and stays at the root.\n\n## What changed\n\nPreviously, `chat()` accepted three generic sampling props directly at the root of its options:\n\n```typescript ignore\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 100,\n})\n```\n\nThese were a convenience layer that the runtime mapped onto whatever the underlying provider expected. That generic mapping is now gone. Sampling parameters live where every other model-specific knob already lives — inside the provider-native `modelOptions` object — under each provider's own canonical key name.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Why it changed\n\n- **Provider-native, single source of truth.** Every provider names these parameters differently — OpenAI's Responses API wants `max_output_tokens`, Anthropic wants `max_tokens`, Gemini wants `maxOutputTokens`, Ollama nests them under `options`. A single generic `maxTokens` prop had to guess the target per provider. Putting them in `modelOptions` means there is exactly one place sampling lives, and it matches the provider's own API surface.\n- **Typed.** `modelOptions` is already typed per adapter+model, so moving sampling there gives you autocomplete and compile-time checking for the exact keys a given model accepts — instead of three loosely-typed root props.\n- **No generic mapping.** Reasoning models in particular do not treat these parameters uniformly (some ignore `temperature`, some reject `max_tokens` below the thinking budget, etc.). A generic root-level mapping papered over those differences; provider-native `modelOptions` lets each adapter handle them honestly.\n\n## Before / after by provider\n\nThe root prop names are the same everywhere (`temperature`, `topP`, `maxTokens`). The `modelOptions` target key differs per provider — use the exact key your provider expects.\n\n### OpenAI\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 100,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Anthropic\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 1024,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n    max_tokens: 1024,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Gemini\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: geminiText('gemini-3.1-pro-preview'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 2048,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { geminiText } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: geminiText('gemini-3.1-pro-preview'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    topP: 0.9,\n    maxOutputTokens: 2048,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Ollama (nested under `options`)\n\nOllama is the one provider where sampling parameters are **nested** inside an `options` object within `modelOptions`, and the token limit is named `num_predict`:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Before\nchat({\n  adapter: ollamaText('llama3'),\n  messages,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  topP: 0.9,\n  maxTokens: 1000,\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { ollamaText } from '@tanstack/ai-ollama'\n\n// After\nchat({\n  adapter: ollamaText('llama3'),\n  messages,\n  modelOptions: {\n    options: {\n      temperature: 0.3,\n      top_p: 0.9,\n      num_predict: 1000,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Provider key reference\n\n| Root prop     | OpenAI              | Anthropic    | Gemini            | Grok         | Groq                    | OpenRouter            | Ollama (nested under `options`) |\n| ------------- | ------------------- | ------------ | ----------------- | ------------ | ----------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `temperature` | `temperature`       | `temperature`| `temperature`     | `temperature`| `temperature`           | `temperature`         | `options.temperature`           |\n| `topP`        | `top_p`             | `top_p`      | `topP`            | `top_p`      | `top_p`                 | `topP`                | `options.top_p`                 |\n| `maxTokens`   | `max_output_tokens` | `max_tokens` | `maxOutputTokens` | `max_tokens` | `max_completion_tokens` | `maxCompletionTokens` | `options.num_predict`           |\n\n## Automated codemod\n\nA jscodeshift codemod moves the root sampling props into `modelOptions` for you, renaming each one to the correct provider-native key. It resolves the provider from the `adapter:` factory call (e.g. `openaiText('gpt-4o')` → OpenAI), so the rewrite is provider-aware. Run it from the repo:\n\n```bash\npnpm codemod:move-sampling-to-model-options \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"\n```\n\nOr run the published transform directly — no clone needed:\n\n```bash\nnpx jscodeshift \\\n  --parser=tsx \\\n  -t https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TanStack/ai/main/codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/transform.ts \\\n  \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"\n```\n\nAdd `--dry --print` to preview the rewrite without modifying files.\n\n**What it does:**\n\n- Targets `chat()`, `ai()`, `generate()`, and `createChatOptions()` calls imported from `@tanstack/ai`.\n- Resolves the provider from the `adapter:` factory call and renames each present root prop to that provider's canonical key.\n- For Ollama, nests the renamed keys inside `modelOptions.options`.\n- Merges into an existing `modelOptions` object literal when present; preserves the original value expressions and expands shorthand props (`{ temperature }` → `temperature: temperature`).\n\n**Report + skip (never partial):** the codemod never partially transforms a call. It leaves the call untouched and emits an `api.report(...)` message when it can't safely proceed:\n\n- **Unresolvable adapter** — no `adapter` prop, the adapter isn't a recognized provider-factory call (e.g. `makeAdapter()`), or it's dynamic/spread.\n- **`modelOptions` is not a plain object literal** — e.g. a spread or an identifier reference.\n- **Key conflict** — a target renamed key already exists in `modelOptions` (or in `modelOptions.options` for Ollama). Resolve these by hand.\n\nSee [`codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/README.md`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/codemods/move-sampling-to-model-options/README.md) for the full transform details and limitations.\n\n## What stays at the root\n\n`metadata` is **not** a sampling parameter and is unaffected — it stays at the root of `chat()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\n\nchat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-4o'),\n  messages,\n  metadata: { requestId: 'abc-123' }, // ← still at the root\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    max_output_tokens: 100,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Need Help?\n\n- [Per-Model Type Safety](../advanced/per-model-type-safety) — how the adapter+model pair drives `modelOptions` inference.\n- [API Reference](../api/ai) — complete `chat()` signature.\n- See your provider's adapter page ([OpenAI](../adapters/openai), [Anthropic](../adapters/anthropic), [Gemini](../adapters/gemini), [Ollama](../adapters/ollama)) for the full list of `modelOptions` it accepts.\n"}
